if (spec == null) return null;
final refusal = _refusal;
if (refusal != null) return refusal;
if (kernel == null) return null;
if (kernel.probed) return kernel.failureNote;
kernel.probed = true;
if (!await kernel.stageVerified()) {
  return kernel.failureNote =
      'fa_cube[${spec.name}]: kernel backend ${kernel.stagingError}';
}
```

Wait — there's a subtle issue here: when `stageVerified()` fails, `kernel.failureNote` is SET but the message template says `'fa_cube[${spec.name}]: kernel backend ${kernel.stagingError}'`. The stagingError already contains 'profile staging failed: ...'. So the note becomes 'fa_cube[name]: kernel backend profile staging failed: ...'. OK.

But notice: in `exec`, the `_kernelErr(kernel.stagingError!)` produces `'fa_cube[name]: kernel backend ${note}'` too. Consistent.

4. Potential race: `updateSpec` while a `stageVerified` in flight... not important.

