11. `effectiveBackend` for a refused spec returns null; documented.

12. AC1 tests: refusal on windows / no-os / no-home. Also env-level background job refusal. Present.

13. Backward compat concern: existing cube specs with `backend: kernel` on Windows/web/limited Linux previously degraded to policy; now they refuse by default. This is the intended behavioral change (the PR's whole point) — docs updated. The PR describes it. Fine.

14. One more: `CubeSpec.parse` — `allowDegrade` check `spec?['allowDegrade']`. `spec` may be null? They call `spec?['allowDegrade']` and later `spec?['backend']`. Note `_checkKeys(spec, ...)` handles null. `allowDegrade != null && allowDegrade is! bool` — strict boolean parse. YAML `yes`/`on` parse as bool in some YAML versions; in Dart yaml package, `yes` is string? yaml 3.x parses only true/false as bool. OK.

Also — `if (allowDegrade) 'allowDegrade': true` in toCanonicalMap. Cache key stability. Good.

15. Now `SandboxedExecutionEnv`: the `effectiveBackend` getter — `_shell.effectiveBackend`. Fine.

16. In `startShellJob`, when prepared == null, error message: `'fa_cube[${spec.name}]: kernel backend ${_shell.kernelStagingError ?? 'profile staging failed'}'`. Note `_shell.kernelStagingError` is `_kernel?.stagingError` — the stagingError from the LAST staging attempt. There's a subtle TOCTOU-ish staleness: prepare returns null ⇒ stagingError just set. OK.

17. What about `exec()` on the env (foreground)? Let me read the full sandboxed_env.dart.

Also, check `agent_cli.dart` for how startupFailure / onWarning / effectiveBackend are used, and whether the refusal surfaces at startup (e.g. a warning at startup). Let me read the relevant part of agent_cli.dart.

